 Joneal runs $5280$ feet on the track of length $50$ feet.  This means Joneal runs $105\frac{6}{5}\cdot$ the entire track.  There are $4 $ quarters of the track, so the track is divided into $16$ equal "quint鹒 Sheets."  This means that Joneal has run $167\frac15$ full sheets, visually unrolled, Let $P$ be the last point Joneal passes on before the mile marker (and let $R$ be the position of $S$).  The angle $\angle RPO$ is $167\frac15^\circ$, so $\alpha, \beta, \gamma$ are all acute angles:
[asy]
unitsize(0.1cm);

basepath=section(50,0.5);

pair S=(0,0);

draw(Circle(S,50),red);

draw(arc(S,51.81,0,130));

dot(S);

label("$R$",S,SE);

